      A: { title: "The Bullet Train", text: "In 1964, Japan opened a new kind of train. People called it the bullet train because it was fast and shaped like a bullet. Today, these trains can go about 320 kilometers per hour. They run on special tracks with no road crossings. This keeps them safe. Bullet trains are also very good at being on time. On average, they are less than one minute late! Every year, hundreds of millions of people ride them. Many other countries now have fast trains too." },
