      A: { title: "The Colosseum", text: "Almost 2,000 years ago, the Romans built a giant stadium in Rome. It is called the Colosseum. About 50,000 people could sit inside to watch shows. Some shows had wild animals like lions and bears. Others had fighters called gladiators. The Romans even had a roof made of cloth to give shade on sunny days. The Colosseum was built in only about ten years. Today, part of it is broken, because of earthquakes and people taking its stones. But it still stands, and millions of tourists visit it every year." },
