      A: { title: "Paintings in Caves", text: "Thousands of years ago, people painted pictures on cave walls. Some of the most famous are in Lascaux, in France. They are about 17,000 years old! The paintings show horses, deer and big cattle. How did people paint in a dark cave? They used small lamps that burned animal fat. They made colors from red and yellow earth and black charcoal. They blew paint through hollow bones to make some shapes. Four teenagers found the Lascaux cave in 1940. They followed their dog into a hole in the ground." },
