      A: { title: "Magellan's Long Voyage", text: "In 1519, Ferdinand Magellan left Spain with five ships and about 270 men. He wanted to sail west to the Spice Islands. The trip was very hard. There were storms, and the men ran out of food. In 1521, the ships reached the Philippines. Magellan died there in a battle at Mactan. The fighters of a local chief named Lapulapu defeated his men. Only one ship made it back to Spain, in 1522. It had just 18 men. But it was the first ship to sail all the way around the world." },
